  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, linked-pile investigation): This item is the umbrella-evidence claim within INV-nanon AND a direct instance of INV-luhur sub-pattern 1 (schema-declares-no-writer): AnalysisRun's lack of edges_emitted/nodes_emitted fields is the writer-contract gap that makes the 61/84 zero-edge condition invisible to provenance consumers. Adding edges_emitted to AnalysisRun would close both halves — making the scan-and-emit-nothing condition both detectable and provenance-queryable. Suggests this item is the natural bridge between INV-nanon and INV-luhur."  # 284c
- op: discuss  # f623
  at: '2026-06-02T06:28:27Z'  # f623
  by: agent  # f623
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f623
  clock: 6  # f623
  nonce: f623  # f623
  message: "Pass-28 INV-bikaj scope-quantification update — 55/84 (65.5%) ARs emit NEITHER nodes NOR edges.\n\nINV-bikaj's existing statement quantifies the edge-only side: \"61 of 84 (72.6%) AnalysisRun passes produce 0 edges\". Pass-28 broadens the measurement to \"0 nodes AND 0 edges\" using `node.origin_run_id` and `edge.origin_run_id` as production-truth indicators:\n\n- **AR emitting nodes**: 19/84 — bash, csharp, database-query-linker, event-sourcing-linker, go, graphql-resolver-linker, html, http-linker, java, javascript, js-module-linker, message-queue-linker, python, rust, solidity, subprocess-linker, swift, websocket-linker, yaml_ansible.\n- **AR emitting edges (any)**: 23/84.\n- **AR emitting edges but no nodes**: 10/84 — containment-linker, decorator-dispatch, dependency-linker, enclosure-linker, inheritance-linker, json, method-call-recovery, pyffi-linker, rust-trait-dispatch-linker, type-hierarchy. (These are pure edge synthesizers.)\n- **AR emitting nothing (no nodes, no edges)**: **55/84 (65.5%)** — airflow-framework-dispatch-linker, annotation-convention-linker, apex, astro, bibtex, bitbake, build-target-linker, controller-routes-linker, crypto-flow-linker, di-resolution, django-orm-dispatch-linker, fennel, gitignore, gleam, go-cobra-linker, go-memberlist-linker, hack, haxe, inherited-calls, ipc-linker, and ~35 more.\n\nTwo cohorts within the 55:\n- **Linker-class, language-applicable but not exercised** (~15-20): ipc-linker, di-resolution, crypto-flow-linker, etc. — Python codebase doesn't exhibit the patterns these linkers detect. Wasted scan.\n- **Analyzer-class, language absent from codebase** (~35-40): apex, astro, bibtex, bitbake, fennel, gleam, hack, haxe, etc. — no source files of that language. Scan finds 0 files, registers an AR with files_analyzed=0, emits nothing. Design-intentional given the no-files state, but the AR record itself is overhead.\n\nINV-bikaj's original statement focused on the high-load edge-zero passes (8 linkers scanning 100+ files for nothing, ~14s wall-clock). Pass-28's broader measurement frames the upper bound: 65.5% of all AR records produce no graph contribution. The 8 high-load passes remain the cost-effective fix targets; the 35-40 absent-language analyzers are cheaper individually but numerous.\n\nStatus: no change. Pass-28 supplies the AR-production breakdown for INV-bikaj's \"true scope\" — INV-bikaj P2 + \"no activation gate\" framing remains correct; the 55-pass measurement is the strictest scope cap.\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass28_probe4.py Q2 / output at /tmp/pass28_output4.log."  # f623
- op: discuss  # f18a
  at: '2026-06-02T06:40:39Z'  # f18a
  by: agent  # f18a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f18a
  clock: 7  # f18a
  nonce: f18a  # f18a
  message: "Pass-29 INV-bikaj — F28.5 producer-emit-zero count reframing: 4 of 18 \"linker-no-fire\" passes actually produce sketch_precomputed output.\n\nPass-28 F28.5 quantified \"55/84 ARs emit NEITHER nodes NOR edges\" using `node.origin_run_id` and `edge.origin_run_id` as production indicators. Pass-29 applied the sibling-field sweep (sub-pattern 8 from pass-27) to AR production attribution and finds 4 of the 18 \"linker-no-fire\" sub-cohort actually contribute to **sketch_precomputed** surfaces:\n\n- **markdown** (113 files, 6070ms, 0 nodes, 0 edges): produces 111 entries in `sketch_precomputed.centrality_scores` (per pass-25 F25.2 / F25.15). The 6.07 seconds of wall-clock IS productive, just not measured by node/edge counters.\n- **toml** (9 files, 232ms): pass-25 F25.15 noted toml AR registers files_analyzed=9 but produces 0 nodes; pass-29 finds toml is one of the markdown/yaml-style passes that may feed sketch_precomputed (need separate verification on substrate; the 1-entry CS .toml from pass-25 F25.2 is consistent with this).\n- **yaml_ansible** (per pass-25 F25.15, files_analyzed=0 but contributes 167 CS .yaml entries — producer attribution is opaque per F26.8).\n- **json** (per pass-25 F25.15, 9 files in / 0 nodes / 1 CS .json entry).\n\nThe reframing: pass-28 F28.5's \"55/84 emit nothing\" framing is **overstated when sketch_precomputed contribution is not counted**. The \"produce nothing\" cohort, narrowed to ARs that contribute to **none** of {nodes, edges, sketch_precomputed.centrality_scores, sketch_precomputed.vocabulary, sketch_precomputed.readme_description, sketch_precomputed.config_info}, is at most 51/84 (subtracting at least 4 surveyed above; may be fewer once full sketch_precomputed attribution is done).\n\nSame finding-family as F28.1 / F27.5 / F26.15: substrate has output at a different field path; the original probe missed it. Sub-pattern (8) sibling-field locations sweep applies to AR-production-counting just as it applies to per-Symbol field coverage.\n\nThe reframing doesn't affect INV-bikaj's underlying concern — \"linkers scanning every file for patterns that aren't present spend O(repo-size) time per pass with no output\" — but it narrows the emit-zero cohort by ~4 ARs and identifies markdown as the most cost-effective targeting candidate (6.07s wall-clock for 111 CS entries that have no per-entry provenance per F26.8).\n\nCohort classification update (replacing pass-28 F28.5's cohort split):\n\n- **Absent-language cohort** (37 ARs, files=0 and duration<100ms): apex, astro, bibtex, bitbake, fennel, gleam, hack, haxe, luau, kdl, prisma, twig, tcl, sparql, jni-linker, tauri-ipc-linker, ... — Design-correct given no source files of those languages exist in the codebase.\n- **Files-analyzed-but-emit-zero-via-nodes/edges** (18 ARs): markdown (6070ms), di-resolution (2353ms), odin (483ms), make (359ms), apex-noinfo (240ms), annotation-convention-linker (240ms), toml (232ms), gitignore (194ms), smithy (134ms), pascal (131ms), wgsl (116ms), janet (107ms), fennel (105ms), sql (67ms), xml (9ms), route-handler-linker, go-cobra-linker, ipc-linker. Of these 18, at minimum 4 (markdown, toml, json, yaml_ansible) contribute to sketch_precomputed.\n\nThe expensive non-fire targets remain:\n- markdown: 6.07s — but is productive (111 CS); separate optimization angle.\n- di-resolution: 2.35s — pure analyzer-time waste (Python codebase doesn't exhibit DI patterns).\n- ~14 more <500ms each.\n\nStatus: no change. Pass-29 supplies the corrected scope and identifies markdown's CS contribution as out-of-scope of INV-bikaj's \"emit nothing\" framing.\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass29_probe2.py Q3 / output at /tmp/pass29_output2.log."  # f18a
- op: discuss  # 49da
  at: '2026-06-02T17:12:08Z'  # 49da
  by: agent  # 49da
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 49da
  clock: 8  # 49da
  nonce: 49da  # 49da
  message: "Pass-34 F34.A4 — `--frameworks all` newly-activated ARs: 6/8 emit nothing, 2/8 emit-with-violations.\n\nProbe ran `hypergumbo run . --frameworks all` and diffed AR set against default substrate. 8 ARs added:\n- 6 with files_analyzed=0 / nodes=0 / edges=0: django-third-party-dispatch-linker, openapi-linker, react-component-linker, view-template-linker, vue-component-linker, vue-template-method-linker\n- 2 with emission AND validation violations:\n  - grpc-linker: 11 nodes, 4 edges (11 id_format violations on Symbol.id format)\n  - graphql-linker: 2 nodes, 0 edges (2 id_format violations on Symbol.stable_id)\n\nINV-bikaj's existing scope is \"61/84 default ARs produce 0 edges\". Pass-34 extends to the framework-linker activation case: 8/8 of these newly-activated ARs emit at most 11 nodes, 6/8 emit nothing, and the 2 that emit do so with writer-contract violations.\n\nThe 6 zero-emitters split into 2 sub-categories:\n1. **Framework-pattern-detector linkers (django-third-party-dispatch, vue-component, vue-template-method, view-template)**: Fail to detect because hypergumbo doesn't expose the framework signatures (no Django models, no Vue components, no Jinja2/etc. templates). files_analyzed=0 means the file-router never routed any file to these linkers.\n2. **Schema-detector linkers (openapi-linker, react-component-linker)**: Same root cause — no OpenAPI spec files, no React components in the corpus.\n\nThis matches pass-28 F28.5's \"55/84 default ARs emit nothing\" mechanism: absent-language sources keep files_analyzed=0 → linker has nothing to dispatch on → 0 emission. The `--frameworks all` flag activates the linkers BUT doesn't provide the source-detection layer they need.\n\nThe 2 emit-with-violations cases (grpc, graphql) reveal that linker activation is correct but the linker bodies (likely test-only patterns matched against test_grpc_linker.py / test_graphql_linker.py) emit nodes whose IDs/stable_ids bypass the canonical Symbol.id factory. So the F34.A1 validation gap (filed at INV-luhur) overlaps the F34.A4 emission gap here: of 8 ARs that ran, the 2 that DID emit ALSO produced violations — a 100% violation rate on flag-activated ARs that emit anything.\n\nFix-path candidate: scope-cap `--frameworks all` to \"all detected frameworks\" (per F34.A3 the catalog dump is unfiltered already; mirror that decision at the linker activation layer). Or surface a warning at run-end: \"8 ARs activated via --frameworks all, 6 produced 0 emission, 2 produced violations; consider removing the flag.\"\n\n**Probe artifact:** `/tmp/p34_outputA2.log` A.14 (per-AR emission table). No status change."  # 49da
- op: discuss  # 9b28
  at: '2026-06-02T17:33:16Z'  # 9b28
  by: agent  # 9b28
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9b28
  clock: 9  # 9b28
  nonce: 9b28  # 9b28
  message: "Pass-35 batch (2 findings — AR pass-set monotone-inclusion across codebases + cli_pkg extreme manifestation).\n\n**F35.B1 — AR pass-set inclusion is monotone across 3 substrates.** Cross-codebase diff matrix:\n```\nROOT (hypergumbo whole-repo):           84 ARs\nTRACKER (hypergumbo-tracker pkg):       66 ARs\nCLI_PKG (packages/hypergumbo CLI pkg):  64 ARs\n3-way intersection:                     64 ARs\nROOT only:                              18 ARs (all non-Python language ARs)\nTRACKER only:                            0 ARs\nCLI_PKG only:                            0 ARs\nROOT∩TRACKER\\CLI_PKG:                    2 ARs\n```\nCLI_PKG (64) ⊂ TRACKER (66) ⊂ ROOT (84). The activation gate's response to source-language presence is correctly monotone — non-Python AR activation only fires when non-Python source files are detected. This is structural positive determinism: 0 spurious ARs in any subset substrate.\n\n**F35.B2 — 64 ARs fire on CLI_PKG's 32-node substrate. Extreme manifestation of INV-bikaj.**\n\nCLI_PKG substrate (packages/hypergumbo CLI pkg):\n- 32 nodes, 22 edges\n- 6 distinct kinds: external_symbol=14, function=6, variable=4, dependency=4, file=3, project=1\n- 64 ARs fire — **2× the node count**\n- Edge types observed: calls=12, imports=6, references=3, module_attr_ref=1\n\nWith only 22 edges across 4 edge types, **at most ~60 of 64 ARs MUST emit zero**. INV-bikaj's existing scope tracks this at default-substrate scale (61/84 ARs produce 0 edges) and pass-28 F28.5 extended (\"55/84 emit nothing\"). Pass-35 finds the extreme: an extremely small codebase activates virtually the full AR pool but ~94% of ARs cannot emit because the corresponding patterns/languages/frameworks don't exist.\n\nPass-34 F34.A4 noted \"6/8 newly-activated --fw all ARs emit nothing\"; pass-35 F35.B2 is the corollary at the codebase-shrinkage axis: the gate doesn't tighten as codebase shrinks.\n\nThis points to a structural opportunity: the file-router could short-circuit AR activation for languages/frameworks completely absent from the codebase BEFORE the AR starts. CLI_PKG has 25 Python + 2 markdown + 5 toml file-level nodes; activating 64 ARs (including all non-Python language analyzers + most framework linkers) is wasted work.\n\nFix-path candidate: pre-AR filter activates only ARs whose declared file-glob has ≥1 match. Would change ROOT's 84 → still 84 (large repo), TRACKER 66 → ~10-12 (Python+toml+markdown only), CLI_PKG 64 → ~8.\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p35_probeB.py` cross-codebase diff probe; `/tmp/p35_outputB.log` (B.9 AR pass-set inclusion). No status change."  # 9b28
- op: discuss  # df96
  at: '2026-06-02T20:45:20Z'  # df96
  by: agent  # df96
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df96
  clock: 10  # df96
  nonce: df96  # df96
  message: "Pass 36 (continuing 06022026_1622) cross-codebase AR-activation delta.\n\nF36.C5: --frameworks all adds 8 ARs to root (84→92) but only 4 ARs to tracker-pkg (66→70). Per-codebase AR-activation rate of framework-linker passes varies. Pass-34 F34.A4's '8/8 emit nothing or violations' headline was root-codebase-specific quantification; tracker doesn't activate the full 8-pass set. Cross-codebase generalization of INV-bikaj: activation gate continues to misfire — passes register and resource-consume on substrates where their language grammar isn't present, but additionally, --frameworks all 'force on' fails to activate the full catalog cross-codebase uniformly. F35.B2's '64 ARs fire on 32-node CLI_PKG' showed the activation-gate problem at extreme scale; F36.C5 shows the same gate's INVERSE flavor: when forced on, doesn't fully fire. Both are mechanism of the activation-gate-not-tightened pattern."  # df96
- op: discuss  # 72a2
  at: '2026-06-02T21:28:29Z'  # 72a2
  by: agent  # 72a2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 72a2
  clock: 11  # 72a2
  nonce: 72a2  # 72a2
  message: "Pass 37 (continuing 06022026_1700) AR-activation enumeration + no-op characterization (2 findings).\n\nF37.D1 (cross-codebase enumeration of --fw all-added passes): root --fw all adds 8 ARs; tracker --fw all adds 4. Specific decomposition:\n  Intersection — UNIVERSAL framework linkers (4): django-third-party-dispatch-linker, graphql-linker, grpc-linker, view-template-linker. Register on both codebases.\n  Root-only — CONTENT-CONDITIONAL framework linkers (4): openapi-linker, react-component-linker, vue-component-linker, vue-template-method-linker. Register only when codebase has matching grammar/file patterns. Tracker package has no openapi specs / React / Vue → not registered.\n  Tracker-only: empty (no AR universal-on-tracker-but-absent-on-root).\nEnumerates pass-36 F36.C5 quantification (+8 root / +4 tracker delta). The 4-vs-4 split (universal vs content-conditional) is a NEW substructure of INV-bikaj.\n\nF37.D2 (7/8 framework-linker --fw all activations are no-op AR slots): files_analyzed quantification:\n  graphql-linker: 860 root / 80 tracker — ONLY framework linker that actually performs file analysis under --fw all\n  All others (django-third-party / grpc / openapi / react / view-template / vue-component / vue-template-method): files_analyzed=0 on both codebases — register, consume AR slot, but do no file-analysis work\nBut: pass-34 F34.A1 shows grpc-linker emits 11 nodes + 11 id_format violations, AND graphql-linker emits 2 nodes + 2 stable_id violations, on root substrate. So 'files_analyzed=0' is NOT equivalent to 'emits nothing' — grpc-linker synthesizes 11 nodes via runtime pattern detection without analyzing files. THREE independent dimensions of 'did this AR do work': (a) AR registered (--fw all activates it), (b) files_analyzed > 0, (c) nodes/edges emitted. F34.A4 was conflating (b) and (c). Mechanism implication for INV-bikaj fix: pre-AR file-glob filter wouldn't catch the synthesizing-from-detection case (grpc); needs separate gate for runtime-pattern-detection vs file-walk activations.\n\nDetailed AR-activation matrix:\n  | AR | root files | tracker files | nodes (per F34) | registered both | enumeration |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | django-third-party-dispatch-linker | 0 | 0 | 0 | Y | universal |\n  | graphql-linker | 860 | 80 | 2 | Y | universal |\n  | grpc-linker | 0 | 0 | 11 | Y | universal |\n  | view-template-linker | 0 | 0 | 0 | Y | universal |\n  | openapi-linker | 0 | n/a | 0 | N (tracker absent) | content-conditional |\n  | react-component-linker | 0 | n/a | 0 | N | content-conditional |\n  | vue-component-linker | 0 | n/a | 0 | N | content-conditional |\n  | vue-template-method-linker | 0 | n/a | 0 | N | content-conditional |"  # 72a2
- op: discuss  # 963f
  at: '2026-06-02T22:16:41Z'  # 963f
  by: agent  # 963f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 963f
  clock: 12  # 963f
  nonce: 963f  # 963f
  message: "Pass 38 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 3 findings batched at cross-codebase AR-activation matrix (scripts/ as 3rd codebase):\n\nF38.D1: F35.B1 monotone-inclusion EXTENDS across 3 substrates. SCRIPTS (63 ARs) ⊂ TRACKER (66 ARs) ⊂ ROOT (84 ARs). Strict subset chain:\n- 3 TRACKER-only ARs vs SCRIPTS: enclosure-linker, markdown, toml (no markdown/.toml files in scripts/; no Python ENC-class nodes)\n- 18 ROOT-only ARs vs TRACKER: language analyzers (csharp/go/html/java/javascript/json/rust/solidity/sql/swift/wgsl/xml) + 6 framework-linker passes (jni / js-module / pyffi / solidity-abi / tauri-ipc / wasm-bindgen)\n- 0 SCRIPTS-only / TRACKER-only ARs (strict subset; no codebase introduces ARs the next-larger doesn't have)\n\nF38.D2: SCRIPTS EP-kind diversity = 2 (main_function=6 + shell_script=29; 35 EPs total). Extends pass-35 F35.C3 cross-codebase EP-kind table to 4 codebases:\n- ROOT: 6 EP-kinds (104 EPs total)\n- TRACKER: 3 EP-kinds (15 EPs total)\n- SCRIPTS: 2 EP-kinds (35 EPs total) — NEW data point\n- CLI_PKG: 1 EP-kind (1 EP total)\nBash-heavy directories surface shell_script EP kind universally; absence of HTTP frameworks → 0 http_route EPs → 0 features (F38.D2 producer chain). EP-kind diversity scales with codebase composition diversity, not size.\n\nF38.D4: scripts/ fa>0 set is 8 ARs (subset of 63 registered): bash + python + 6 generic-pattern linkers (event-sourcing, message-queue, graphql-resolver, http, subprocess, database-query). The route-handler-linker + websocket-linker are REGISTERED on scripts but produce fa=0 (no matching files/patterns). Refines pass-37 F37.D1+D2 cross-codebase enumeration: F37.D2 named 3 dimensions (registered / files_analyzed>0 / nodes-edges-emitted); F38.D4 adds a 4th dimension — pass-set-included. SCRIPTS surfaces the in-pass-set-but-fa=0 case. The full 4-axis 'AR-did-work' matrix:\n(a) Registered in catalog\n(b) In substrate's analysis_runs[] pass-set\n(c) files_analyzed > 0\n(d) symbols/edges emitted\n\nscripts/ shows (b)-but-not-(c) for route-handler-linker, websocket-linker. Tracker shows the SAME (b)-but-not-(c) for some content-conditional linkers. Pass-37 F34.A4's '8/8 emit nothing/violations' headline already covered the (a)-but-not-(c) case for framework-linker passes; F38.D4 extends to 'always-in-pass-set linkers fail (c) on bash-heavy codebases'. Fix-path candidate: pre-AR activation gate that drops linker from AR record when source file presence absent (parallel to F37.D2 'pre-AR file-glob filter'). Currently the AR is emitted at fa=0 with no signal that it should have been skipped."  # 963f
- op: discuss  # 8f42
  at: '2026-06-02T22:51:56Z'  # 8f42
  by: agent  # 8f42
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8f42
  clock: 13  # 8f42
  nonce: 8f42  # 8f42
  message: "Pass 39 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 4 findings batched at 4th-codebase AR-activation matrix (htrac-frontend as TS-only frontend):\n\nF39.C1 (CORRECTS F38.D1): Monotone-inclusion chain BREAKS at HTRAC. Pass-38 claimed SCRIPTS(63) ⊂ TRACKER(66) ⊂ ROOT(84). With HTRAC added: HTRAC has 66 ARs but is NOT a subset of TRACKER. HTRAC-only ARs vs TRACKER: html / javascript / js-module-linker / json — present because HTRAC has 1 HTML file, 1 JS file, 2 JSON files. TRACKER lacks these source-file types. So F38.D1 'strict subset chain' claim only holds for codebases of similar composition (Python+bash). REVISED: AR pass-set is composition-conditional. Each codebase's pass-set is union of (a) framework-agnostic analyzers + (b) language analyzers whose file-glob has ≥1 match. ROOT is superset because it contains all language file types; pairwise subset relations only hold when one codebase's language set ⊂ other's.\n\nF39.C3: HTRAC EP-kind diversity = 2 (script_module=5 + html_entry=1; 6 EPs total). Extends F38.D2 4-codebase EP-kind table:\n- ROOT: 6 kinds (104 EPs)\n- TRACKER: 3 kinds (15 EPs)\n- SCRIPTS: 2 kinds (35 EPs) — {main_function, shell_script}\n- HTRAC: 2 kinds (6 EPs) — {script_module, html_entry}\nSame diversity number as SCRIPTS but COMPLETELY DISJOINT kind sets. Each codebase has distinctive EP-kind footprint reflecting language/role composition. EP-kind discovery vocabulary is fully content-conditional.\n\nF39.C4: HTRAC features=0 (TS-only frontend; no HTTP route handlers). Reinforces F36.B2 + F38.A1 framing 'features = handler-slice output'. No HTTP routes = no features. 4-codebase features count: ROOT 16, TRACKER 16, SCRIPTS 0, HTRAC 0 — split is whether codebase has a backend HTTP route surface (orthogonal to size).\n\nF39.C5: HTRAC fa>0 includes websocket-linker (1 file analyzed — ws-client.ts). Content-conditional fa>0 confirmed at 3rd codebase, refining F38.D4. The 4-axis 'AR-did-work' matrix:\n- (a) registered in catalog\n- (b) in 84-AR pass-set (codebase-composition-dependent per F39.C1)\n- (c) files_analyzed > 0\n- (d) nodes/edges emitted\n\nHTRAC: bash AR is REGISTERED + IN-PASS-SET but fa=0 (no bash files in HTRAC). websocket-linker fires + emits content (TS WS code present). Per-language activation gate refines per F39.C1 — it's not just 'pre-AR file-glob filter' (F37.D2 fix-path proposal); it's 'AR membership in pass-set should be composition-conditional from the start'."  # 8f42
