  nonce: '72e1'  # 72e1
  message: "Pass-40 F40.C2+C5 batch — DOCS as 5th codebase data point + features=http_route-projection cross-codebase.\n\nF40.C2: DOCS substrate adds 5th codebase data point. Cross-codebase table updated:\n| codebase | nodes | AR count | EPs | features | INV-bazij% |\n| ROOT (s21) | 34253 | 84 | 104 | 16 | 0.84 |\n| TRACKER | 4959 | 66 | 15 | 16 | 0.81 |\n| SCRIPTS | ~250 | 63 | 35 | 0 | 7.0 BREACH |\n| HTRAC | 77 | 66 | 3 | 0 | 16.88 BREACH |\n| CLI_PKG | 32 | 64 | 1 | 0 | 0.0 |\n| **DOCS | 2861 | 63 | 0 | 0 | 0.38 NEW** |\n\nDOCS fa>0 set = 2 ARs of 63 registered (markdown, json). 61 are no-ops. AR pass-set composition observation: DOCS (63) and SCRIPTS (63) converge at the same AR count from different compositions — suggests these are baseline 'always-registered' passes with minimal content-conditional additions on minimal-content codebases. TRACKER and HTRAC at 66 ARs add 3 content-conditional passes each. ROOT at 84 adds 21 more (mostly framework linkers).\n\nF40.C2 refinement of F37.D2/F38.D4 'AR-did-work' hierarchy on DOCS: registered=63 ⊃ pass-set-included (full)=63 ⊃ fa>0=2 (markdown, json) ⊃ emits-nodes=1 (markdown emits 2859, json emits 0). The json AR fires on YAML files but emits 0 nodes — separate (fa>0, ne=0) cell distinct from the 'fa=0 always no-op' case. Adds nuance: fa>0 doesn't imply emission.\n\nF40.C5: features=http_route-projection generalizes across all 6 codebases. With ROOT 16 features / 8 http_route EPs and TRACKER 16 features / unknown route count, the four other codebases (SCRIPTS / HTRAC / CLI_PKG / DOCS) all have features=0, matching their 0 http_route EP counts. No codebase shows features without http_route EPs. Generalizes pass-34 F34.B1's ROOT-specific claim to a robust cross-codebase invariant: **features ⟺ http_route EPs present**. Cleaner cross-codebase confirmation than the within-flag substrate-comparison from passes 34-37."  # 72e1
